  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe Heidenhain Klartext post (`assets/posts/heidenhain-klartext.cps`) writes the drilling and tapping cycles and the dwell for the iTNC 530 NC 340490-03 (the Fehlmann Picomax 55 profile). Before this change, the post refused each cycle and each dwell.\n\n| Stream cycle | Posted |\n|---|---|\n| DRILL, SPOT | `CYCL DEF 200 DRILLING` (Q200, Q201, Q206, Q202 = the whole depth, Q210 = 0, Q203, Q204 = Q200, Q211 = the dwell), then `CYCL CALL` |\n| PECK, DEEP | the checked chain as `L` blocks (the #4224 precedent). No cycle 205 or 203. |\n| TAP, rigid | `CYCL DEF 207 RIGID TAPPING NEW` (Q200, Q201, Q239 = feed / rpm, Q203, Q204) |\n| TAP, floating holder | `CYCL DEF 206 TAPPING NEW` (Q200, Q201, Q206, Q211, Q203, Q204) |\n| the dwell of PECK or DEEP | `CYCL DEF 9.0 DWELL TIME` and `CYCL DEF 9.1 DWELL <s>` after the feed to the depth |\n\n- The parameter set is the resolver's `drillC200` level `q211` (no Q395; no Q208 or Q395 on cycle 205 either, because the post writes no cycle 205).\n- The post defines a cycle again only when its words change. Each hole gets one `CYCL CALL`, with the tool at R over the hole.\n- The post compares each chain move that a native cycle replaces with the motion of that cycle. A chain that differs is refused by name. Thus the native cycle does the motion that the simulation and the gouge check read.\n- The post now accepts the tool kinds `drill` and `tap`. A drill or a tap cuts only inside its drilling cycle (a drill feeds only along the hole axis). A tapping cycle needs a tap tool.\n- The post declares `floatingTapping = true`.\n- The other output of the Picomax stays byte-identical: the `picomax.nc` golden and the refusal goldens did not change. The new code is below `onOpen`, so the script line numbers in the refusal goldens are the same.\n- The DIN/ISO post `heidenhain.cps` did not change (#4226 works there).\n\nExample (from the new golden `picomax_cycles.nc`):\n\n```\n30 L X+5 Y+5 Z+6 R0 FMAX\n31 CYCL DEF 200 DRILLING ~\n  Q200=+1 ~\n  Q201=-10 ~\n  Q206=+100 ~\n  Q202=+10 ~\n  Q210=+0 ~\n  Q203=+5 ~\n  Q204=+1 ~\n  Q211=+0.5\n32 CYCL CALL\n...\n79 L X+15 Y-5 Z-5 R0 F100\n80 CYCL DEF 9.0 DWELL TIME\n81 CYCL DEF 9.1 DWELL 0.3\n...\n104 CYCL DEF 207 RIGID TAPPING NEW ~\n  Q200=+1 ~\n  Q201=-8 ~\n  Q239=+1 ~\n  Q203=+5 ~\n  Q204=+1\n105 CYCL CALL\n```\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/4227-klartext-cycles.md`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\nBinary `script_heidenhain_klartext` (crate `camcraft-post`), new module `crates/post/tests/klartext/cycle_tests.rs` (it joins the existing suite; no new test binary):\n- `cycle_tests::klartext_cycles_post_on_the_picomax_golden` (new golden `crates/post/tests/recorded/golden/heidenhain-klartext/picomax_cycles.nc`, stream `crates/post/tests/klartext/cycles.cnc`)\n- `cycle_tests::drill_posts_cycle_200_with_the_whole_depth_and_the_dwell_at_depth`\n- `cycle_tests::peck_and_deep_post_the_checked_chain_and_deep_dwells_with_cycle_9`\n- `cycle_tests::rigid_and_floating_taps_post_cycles_207_and_206`\n- `cycle_tests::each_klartext_cycle_refusal_names_its_cause` (BORE, a cycle not at R, a chain that is not the cycle's motion, a tap cycle with a drill, a rigid tap dwell, a floating tap dwell above 0.5 s, a drill feed outside its cycle, a depth that differs from the chain)\n- `cycle_tests::rigid_tapping_is_refused_on_a_machine_without_it`\n- `milling_cutter_kinds_are_explicit_and_incompatible_tools_refuse_the_cli_save` (changed: drill and tap are refused outside a drilling cycle)\n\n## Gate results\n\nAll results are on head `0ea1e7701f51886461703aa61a80b52f920112dd`.\n\n- winbuild (`lanes --needs post`): `cargo test -p camcraft-post --test script_heidenhain_klartext`: 35 passed, 0 failed. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- mac-1 (`lanes --needs app --pool`): `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 167 steps, all ok. These steps include the post suites, `conformance`, `klartext_builtin` and the example catalog suites `example_catalog` (28 s), `example_catalog_adaptive` and `example_catalog_edge_work`, and `first_part_programs`.\n- mac-1: `cargo xtask gate light --base origin/main`: 6 steps, all ok.\n- No heavy step (P6).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The program did not run on the control.\n- The Klartext reader of PR #4361 is not on `main`. Thus there is no round-trip test through the reader. The reader reads cycle 200 and `CYCL CALL`. It does not read cycles 206 and 207 or the old-style cycle 9 blocks.\n- The Picomax machine file states no `rigid_tapping`. The post writes cycle 207 when the machine does not state `false`, as the DIN/ISO post does with G207. The decision file says how to refuse it.\n- The refusals for a cycle 200 level other than `q211` and for a dwell form other than cycle 9 cannot occur while the post accepts only NC 340490-03.\n\nChangelog: The Heidenhain Klartext post writes drilling (cycle 200), rigid tapping (cycle 207), floating tapping (cycle 206) and the dwell (cycle 9) for the iTNC 530 NC 340490-03; peck and deep holes post as explicit moves.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #4227\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
